                <pb facs="0293" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg159"/>

                <head>No. 116.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 11,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 596.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to Mr. Hosmer’s
                    dispatch No. 817, of the 5th ultimo, in relation to the Spanish Central American
                    line of steamrers and Costa Rica, I have to request you to furnish to the
                    Department as full information as possible in regard to the contracts of the
                    German and English line of steamers referred to in your correspondence with the
                    Costa Rican minister for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
